  "narrative": "The seven new discovery results (H38–H44) complete the interaction batteries for stage IV and ECOG PS≥2, testing whether the four large (~18% relative) accepted findings are independent or collinear. All seven interactions are null or sub-threshold relative to the 10% clinical significance threshold.\n\n**Stage IV interaction battery (H38–H40):**\n- H38 (stage IV × NLR): estimate -0.0033, CI [-0.019, 0.012]. Null. The stage IV effect is not confounded by NLR status.\n- H39 (stage IV × CRP): estimate +0.0086, CI [-0.014, 0.031]. Null. The stage IV effect is not confounded by CRP status.\n- H40 (stage IV × pembrolizumab): estimate -0.0015, CI [-0.019, 0.016]. Null. The stage IV effect is not confounded by treatment assignment.\nAll three mirror the null pattern from the NLR and CRP interaction batteries (H14–H24, H29, H31–H32). Stage IV is an independent structured signal.\n\n**ECOG PS≥2 interaction battery (H41–H44):**\n- H41 (ECOG PS≥2 × NLR): estimate -0.0011, CI [-0.023, 0.021]. Null.\n- H42 (ECOG PS≥2 × CRP): estimate -0.0169, CI [-0.048, 0.014]. Null (CI spans zero; point estimate is 0.7% relative).\n- H43 (ECOG PS≥2 × stage IV): estimate -0.0104, CI [-0.033, 0.013]. Null. This is the most critical test: if the counterintuitive ECOG PS≥2 effect were driven by shared variance with stage IV, this interaction would be significant. It is not.\n- H44 (ECOG PS≥2 × pembrolizumab): estimate -0.0003, CI [-0.025, 0.024]. Null.\nAll four interactions are null. The counterintuitive ECOG PS≥2 effect (H37) is not an artifact of collinearity with NLR, CRP, stage IV, or treatment assignment. It stands as an independent, statistically confirmed association, albeit biologically unexplained.\n\n**Conclusion:** The four large effects (NLR≥3, CRP≥10, stage IV, ECOG PS≥2) are independent. No interaction exceeds the 10% clinical significance threshold. The investigation of the main-effect and interaction landscape for all testable binary variables is complete. The only remaining uncertainty is the biological mechanism behind the counterintuitive directions of H13 (NLR) and H37 (ECOG PS≥2), and the untestable continuous research signatures (A, B, C). These do not warrant further analysis given the current framework.\n\n**Validation:** I request independent validation for H37 (ECOG PS≥2, direction +1). This is the most uncertain finding due to its counterintuitive direction. Independent confirmation will strengthen the conclusion that the effect is real and not a data construction artifact. H13 was similarly counterintuitive and was validated; H37 warrants the same rigor.",
